cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ambit in research or reference it in a standard, please cite it."
title: "Ambit: a capability graph for agent infrastructure"
abstract: >-
  Ambit discovers the capabilities implicit in an agent stack's configuration and
  models them as a graph of goals, capabilities, providers, resources, authority,
  and evidence. It treats what a system can do and what it may do as separate
  objects, records what a system became able to do over time, and makes human
  approval a dependency a plan cannot route around. A capability is not something
  configured; it is an action the system has evidence it can perform.
